# RVV wrappers

Kernels in `lib/` must not call `__riscv_*` or include `<riscv_vector.h>`.

Use [`lib/include/riscv_wrappers.hpp`](lib/include/riscv_wrappers.hpp) (`namespace rvv`). Names describe the operation (`LoadStridedF32M4`, `MergeF32M4`, `GatherF32M4`), not the ISA mnemonic.

When a kernel needs an intrinsic that is not wrapped yet:

1. Add an `inline` wrapper in `riscv_wrappers.hpp` with a readable name and a one-line comment if the mapping is not obvious.
2. Call only that wrapper from the kernel.

```cpp
// BAD
vfloat32m4_t x = __riscv_vlse32_v_f32m4(p, stride, vl);
__riscv_vsse32_v_f32m4(p, stride, x, vl);

// GOOD
rvv::F32M4 x = rvv::LoadStridedF32M4(p, stride, vl);
rvv::StoreStridedF32M4(p, stride, x, vl);
```

`ref::` stays scalar. Do not include the wrappers from `test/reference/`.
